    ],
    "main_argument_chains": [
      {
        "claim": "A logistic rate and a cut at half the inherent growth rate give the carbon total. Equation 3 sets the sequestration rate equal to the felled stock, and equation 4 prints the intensity as r over 2. The annual cut stabilizes at 2 Mt, that is 3.2 times 10 to the 6 cubic meters, with no conversion factor printed, and strong policy reaches neutrality about 2063. Equation 12 writes this year stock inside its own update. Three temperature zones settle at 5 times 10 to the 6 cubic meters, and Table 4 stacks two planting costs on one row. Tien Shan carbon settles at 11 times 10 to the 7 tons. The summary profit is 1.52 times 10 to the 8 dollars, and the body says about 1.5 to 1.55 times 10 to the 8. The cut settles at 5.2 times 10 to the 6 against a prose demand of 4.13 times 10 to the 6, while Table 5 prints that demand as 413.86 cubic meters. The newspaper compares each logging limit with itself.",
        "support_steps": [
          "Set the intensity to r over 2 and equate a rate to a stock",
          "Call 2 Mt the same as 3.2 million cubic meters",
          "Put this year stock inside the recurrence and print wp",
          "Land three zones on one volume and stack two planting costs",
          "Print 413.86 cubic meters in the table and 4.13 million in the prose"
        ],
        "decision_consequence": "Cut Tien Shan old trees every year and replant the felled area, and do not treat 413.86 cubic meters and 4.13 million cubic meters as one demand.",
        "source_pages": [
          7,
          12,
          17,
          19,
          23
        ]
      }
    ],
